\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Title optimization can really increase impressions and clicks. This is the most important attribute of your feed that you can control.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Word order matters - keep the most important keywords in front of title. Google only reads 150 Characters and titles shown in the SERP can cut off at 30 characters.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Consider how people are searching for your products? Do people search for the Brand first? Do they search model or part numbers? Do they search by product type or category?\
